Hello;

I don't boot from ARC, so I'm not a MILO user, but unless you have a
typo in your mail message, 

Illodius wrote:
> 
> to load up the milo prompt all is well. I then "boot fd0:vmlinux.gz
> root:/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1 prompt_ramdisk=1" and it starts to uncompress
  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^

should be 

  root=/dev/fd0

Note the equals as opposed to the colon...  that should get the
install started.  

Also, you should be able to get rid of prompt_ramdisk=1 .  It should
prompt you by itself.  So try this from the MILO prompt:

boot fd0:/vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

BTW, Disk Druid at least used to be problematic, I dunno if it works
any better for Alpha-folk now (maybe it does?).  You might want to use
fdisk for partitioning to be on the safe side, though.

Cheers,
Craig
