On Sun, 2 May 1999, The MaDd0k wrote:

> I just started writing a raytracer, but when I run it, it causes
> unaligned traps.
> 
> Could anyone tell me if there are special things to do to prevent
> that ?
> Are there some tricks to use within data structures or classes declaration ?
> Or maybe something else ?
> 
> I really want my program ot be 64 bits clean ;)


It is not so much a 64 bit cleanliness issue - somewhere you have an
integer, double or something similar which isn't aligned on its natural
alignment, that is integers should be sitting on a boundary of 4 bytes -
managing not to do this actually takes quite a bit of work in C/C++ !

Intel boxes cope with non-aligned accesses in hardware - but I suspect it
slows them down a little.  Alpha boxes do it in software  so it is even
slower.

I think you'll find the addresses you see in your logs should help you
figure out where in your code your doing it.

Dave

