I do not want to start a flamewar about mp3 encoders but all encoders apart
from l3enc from FHG/IIS are no good at 128kbps ... so I understand his wish
to be able to use l3enc. And since FHG/IIS seems to be very ignorand about
user's wishes (I mailed them three times by now with no answer) I do not
think we will ever see a Linux-Alpha native version of it.
And back to the encoders: All more or less free encoders, which include
bladeenc, lamer, 8Hz, etc., are based on the same ISO reference code and are
only optimized for some speed. No work has yet been done by anyone on
quality. The only encoder I know of which has some quality additions is
"encode" from
  ftp://wopr.campus.luth.se:/pub/mpeg_layer_3/
version pre-2.0. Andreas Johansson has added layer 3 joint-stereo and a
quality switch (try -q 99.9) to the ISO code. This improves quality a bit
but is IMHO still not usable for 128kbps.
And back to some more on-topic issues: Andreas also owns an Alpha is
