Thanks a lot to all who helped me with their advice. I borrowed an S3 Virge
card and tried it in my UDB, although it was 2 cm too long (I took the
floppy and internal hard drive away to make room for the card.) The machine
runs under 5.1, I used MILO from 5.2 and compiled 2.0.36 kernel from 5.2
updates without TGA support, and had ARC, MILO, kernel and text console on
the new card. I was able to run X with 1024x768 at 16 bpp, and it was
indeed a big difference with respect to 8 bit TGA colours (GIMP displays
all right now). I tried both S3 and SVGA servers, both worked and I did not
notice any considerable difference. 

Now it remains to find a shorter card...
			
					Roman Martonak.			
