I finally looked up some info on the DS10. It is a DS20(Goldrush) with 1
CPU. Here is an updated table of names and properties that I know of. Each
class (Goldrush/Monet/Clipper) use different motherboards.

DS10, DS20 (Goldrush) - 1CPU vs. 2 CPUs.
XP1000 (Monet) - 1 CPU
ES40 (Clipper) - 1-4 CPUs.

 Brick - Uni, no daughter card 466MHz CPU 75MHz bus
 DP264 - Uni/Dual, daugher cards have CPU and cache, 500MHz CPU 83MHz bus
 Monet - Uni, daughter card has core logic, CPU and cache. 500MHz CPU 83MHz
         bus.
 Clipper - 1-4 CPUs, daughter card has CPU/cache, CPU=500MHz 83MHz bus.


If there is any more confusion, ask away and I'll try to help.

