Robert Bowles wrote:
> 
> I'm assuming that a DU-3.2c passwd-db is _very_ different
> (doesn't use crypt)...

IIRC some old experience this assumption is wrong.  I mean that
apart of a database also exists /etc/passwd and is using a regular
crypt so it is possible to copy-and-paste between Linux and DU
(make sure that you use vipw on DU side - it does more than simple
locking).

This does not exclude, of course, a possibility that some other
password maitenance schemes on DU do exist; also on Linux side one
may use some alternative PAM module (pam_smb, for example, to
authenticate from NT server) so there is no guarantee that the
same encryption will be used on both ends.  OTOH it is really
simple to check if this is the case in some particular situation
just using few accounts with known passwords.

  Michal


