Content-Type: text

> 
> I have a Multia running kernel 2.2.7 (redhat 5.2) with a SCSI tape device.
> If I compile 'st' as a module, I can't do anything with it, eg:
> 
> [root@spanky /root]# insmod st
> Detected scsi tape st0 at scsi0, channel 0, id 1, lun 0
> Unable to get major 9 for SCSI tapes
> /lib/modules/2.2.7/scsi/st.o: init_module: Device or resource busy
....
> 
> Anyone know why this might be?

Standard Red Hat setup when it detects a tape device and a tape
module inserts it to prevent auto-deletion (the idea is not to release
tape buffers in case this module is auto removed).  You likely have this
module already "in" hence "Device or resource busy".  Try 'lsmod' and
check what 'dmesg' has to say.

The next problem is that mt-0.5, as distributed in Red Hat 5.2, is
broken.  Recompile sources, like mt-0.5b, to be found on regular
servers.

  Michal


