Your MILO disk should be just standard FAT format. If you're using rawrite
then make sure you're rawriting the image file (from /milo/images), not 
the just the MILO iteself (from /milo).

NT/Dos should be able to read the MILO floppy w/o any trouble. The kernel
and ramdisk images are different, and NT/Dos won't be able to read them.

