> > I switched to the `generic decchip' driver (de4x5) because of such
> > problems. Works flawlessly for me - with a 5m patch cable.
> > The only problem I have: The onboard chip is unable to cope with the
> > 30m cable which at the moment connects me to my hub, it cycles 100mb /
> > TP / not connected. With a card with a 21140 I have no such problems.
> > Did anyone else experience something like this? Does the 21143 have
> > weak output drivers?
> 
> As I said above I was in contact with Donald Becker because of the
> problems with 21143. tulip.c is the right driver (I tried de4x5 too but
> it doesn't work--I need 100Mbit full duplex). It seems not to be a general
> problem of the 21143 chip. People are reporting it runs with NT ok.

There's a problem with the crystal on the original UX boards that causes
autosensing to be problematic at best. I've found that verison 0.89H of
the driver is fairly reliable, though I have yet to try the latest
version.

You can also look into replacing the crystal. I think if you search
through axp-list there's a message about which crystal to buy etc....

--rdp

