>
> I checked more carefully what was going on. There was actually no error
> with applix. It looks like my menus in Window Maker are not linked to
> the right path... If I put the full path to execute applix
> /opt/bin/applix
> it works fine.... (Due to the way I partitionned my disk a year ago,
> I had to put applix in a non standard directory...).
> Maybe the other person on the list had the same problem.

THAT'S what the problem was.  I put Applix under /usr/local/lib during
installation (there's no opt partition on my machine, and there's not
enough room in the root to create a large enough directory).  I believe I
changed the path in the menu file.

An uneducated guess as to what happened...

Applix installation may not be altering the menu file.  Instead, the
standard path (inside /opt) may be set as a default in the menu file when
X is installed.  I similarly saw a default path for Netscape in the same
file, though Netscape is not installed on my machine.

Maybe Applix installation is supposed to update the menu file and
malfunctioned, or maybe the updating is meant to be left up to the user.
It may or may not be feasible to include an menu-updating feature in the
Applix installation process.  I have very little experience with these
files and don't know how standard the code is.

Bottom line, everything is cool.

John Clayton


